      "shape": "quote-frame",
      "text": "Let P be a regular 101-gon of circumradius 1. Draw each diagonal of P with probability 0.001. This splits P into several closed regions. Let E be the expected value of the perimeter of the region containing the center of P. Compute ⌊10⁹ E⌋."
    },
    {
      "page": 9,
      "shape": "quote-frame",
      "text": "There are unique constants C, α, β such that the number of solutions to the equation ab + 1 = cde with a, b, c, d, e ∈ ℕ with ab ≤ x is asymptotic to Cx^α log^β x as x → ∞. Compute ⌊1000C⌋."
    },
    {
      "page": 9,
      "shape": "TextBox 5",
      "text": "日本語訳：正整数a,b,c,d,eについて、ab＋1＝cde、ab≤xの解の個数が、x→∞でCx^α(log x)^βに漸近する一意な定数C,α,βがある。⌊1000C⌋を求める。"
    },
    {
      "page": 14,
      "shape": "answer",
      "text": "正解：√3/36 ＋ (√3/6) exp(−20√3 − 1/6)"
    },
    {
      "page": 40,
      "shape": "quote-frame",
      "text": "Construct a degree 19 polynomial p(x) ∈ ℂ[x] such that X := {p(x) = p(y)} ⊂ ℙ¹ × ℙ¹ has at least 3 (but not all linear) irreducible components over ℂ. Choose p(x) to be odd, monic, have real coefficients and linear coefficient −19 and calculate p(19)."
    }
